<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#alake-of-egbaland">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alake of Egbaland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alake of Egbaland is the paramount traditional ruler of the Egba, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba people</a> whose capital is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeokuta">Abeokuta</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. The title was originally that of the ruler of Ake, one of the old Egba townships; after the founding of Abeokuta the Alake became, from 1854, the leading ruler of the united Egba. Under British rule after 1914 the office remained an important traditional authority.</p></div>
